# Grid B — U5 Test coverage (does a specific code path have a test?)
#
# Gap target: boolean-shape question about test existence. The answer
# must either cite a specific test function name (proving the LLM
# found it) or explicitly say "no test" (proving it looked and came
# up empty). A hedge like "probably / likely" is dispositive of not
# having actually looked.
#
# Ground truth: runTaskGraph has scheduler_test.go coverage. The
# stall-forces-finalize branch is a specific edge case — whether it
# has a dedicated test is a factual lookup. Regardless of the
# answer, the response must name the test file or clearly state
# absence.
ID="u5b"
NAME="test coverage — runTaskGraph stall-forces-finalize path"
QUESTION="Does runTaskGraph's stall-forces-finalize fallback path (the branch described in CLAUDE.md as 'scheduler stall forces one finalize dispatch so the task always terminates') have a dedicated unit test? If yes, which test file and function?"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC `runTaskGraph` was the
# question's keyword — bar = "复述题目". Tighten by requiring the
# answer to surface either (a) a specific *_test.go file path AND
# the test function name, OR (b) the explicit "no test" / "无测试"
# verdict — proving the LLM actually looked rather than hedged.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="runTaskGraph"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(_test\.go.*Test[A-Z][a-zA-Z]+|no.*test|没有.*测试|尚无.*测试|无.*覆盖)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="probably likely assumption"
